message: >-
  If you use this software, datasets, trained models, or results in your
  research, please cite both the software repository and the associated
  research article.

title: Neural-network analysis of XAS and XMCD spectra for spin and orbital angular momentum prediction

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Ueno
    given-names: Tetsuro

version: 1.0.0

date-released: 2026-10-15

license: MIT

repository-code: https://github.com/teueno/nn-xmcd-angular-momentum

url: https://github.com/teueno/nn-xmcd-angular-momentum

doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23409837

keywords:
  - X-ray absorption spectroscopy
  - XAS
  - X-ray magnetic circular dichroism
  - XMCD
  - machine learning
  - neural network
  - spin angular momentum
  - orbital angular momentum
  - Quanty

abstract: >-
  This software provides a reproducible workflow for preparing,
  auditing, splitting, preprocessing, training, and evaluating
  neural-network models that simultaneously predict spin and orbital
  angular momentum from simulated XAS and XMCD spectra. The workflow
  supports Fe d6, Co d7, and Ni d8 systems and records fixed data
  splits, preprocessing statistics, training histories, evaluation
  metrics, predictions, file hashes, and software-version metadata.

